    "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Yoruiopz/Codex-Blender-Bridge/tarball/v0.4.0",
    "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/Yoruiopz/Codex-Blender-Bridge/zipball/v0.4.0",
    "body": "Blender Codex Bridge **0.4.0 alpha** adds bounded artist plans, protected scope and target verification, quaternion transforms, modeling/UV/paint tools, weight and animation foundations, cooperative jobs, and approved-path GLB/FBX export foundations. It contains **266 MCP tools**. Capabilities retain their documented ownership and context limits.\n\nThis is a development prerelease. **The full artist-workflow 1.0 target is incomplete; all fourteen stable requirements remain open. Windows compatibility work and testing are deferred and unverified.** No merge into `main` is part of this release.\n\nValidated source: [`4470d88bb4d8fb1ed75e86090dd6886fb55eb589`](https://github.com/Yoruiopz/Codex-Blender-Bridge/commit/4470d88bb4d8fb1ed75e86090dd6886fb55eb589), tree `0353d119fd44ac918dc66d871ef2279576f9312d`.\n\n- [Exact-commit CI](https://github.com/Yoruiopz/Codex-Blender-Bridge/actions/runs/40058140088): seven jobs passed; each Python 3.10\u20133.12 \u00d7 MCP SDK 2.0.0/2.2.0 cell passed **7,582 tests**, with three Windows-only skips. Lint, typing, tool inventory and package checks passed.\n- Selected isolated Linux Blender **4.5.14 LTS** (`62c1db4208e8`) and **5.2.2 LTS** (`d13f752e3b9c`) cases passed: UV boundary prerequisites, weight operations, and fresh-process GLB/FBX fixture export/reimport. These checks do not establish a public UV Edit Mode guard, complete delivery content/materials, visual quality, native undo or full workflow acceptance.\n- The exact packaged add-on passed a bounded fresh-candidate \u2192 published 0.3.0 \u2192 upgrade \u2192 rollback probe in one process on each Linux build, including loopback reconnect and default permission denial. Blender restart, preferences migration and installed artist scenarios A\u2013F remain unverified.\n- The exact wheel was installed into a fresh prefix and tested through an actual fresh MCP stdio session: 266 exact public tools, 25 disabled domains, 195 malformed-input responses, schemas/defaults and installed source/RECORD integrity. This was registration/validation coverage, not MCP-to-Blender workflow acceptance.\n\n**Important restrictions:** `project.save` remains unavailable for Save and Save As; protected capture and shader-interface REMOVE/conversion remain unsupported; typed asset import remains quarantined on the known Blender 5.2.2 build. Arbitrary Python stays disabled by default. Neither retained buffers nor global undo history provide durable backups. Native full-inventory, reviewed appearance, constrained-memory and complete A\u2013F acceptance remain outstanding. The declared Blender 4.2 minimum is metadata, not qualification of every patch or platform.\n\nInstall the attached add-on ZIP without extracting it, install the matching MCP wheel, and update the optional Codex plugin together. Restart Blender and the MCP client, recreate session references/previews/baselines, and start with inspection. Use disposable scenes or project copies and retain normal backups. A software rollback does not undo scene edits or exported files. [Candidate installation and limits](https://github.com/Yoruiopz/Codex-Blender-Bridge/blob/4470d88bb4d8fb1ed75e86090dd6886fb55eb589/docs/releases/0.4.0.md).\n\n`SHA256SUMS.txt` verifies the three exact CI-built packages. `EVIDENCE-SHA256SUMS.txt` verifies the retained development-evidence archive, which contains original reports/logs, source-specific failed attempts, all six matrix artifacts and an independently restored/fsck-verified source Git bundle. The evidence archive is for audit, not an installer. Earlier releases and assets remain available unchanged.\n"
  },
